# Item 739, its result side: l2_mad_call hands the walk an int result only, so at the root a held
# callable whose header result is not int -- `fn: (size_t: x) size_t` here -- is refused, located.
# Before slice 13 of the implements port the int-typed result met this size_t place as a refused
# conversion; after it, and before this row, the root wrapped the mistyped value in an int -> size_t
# edge and the walk failed at run time.  Mutant: no result check -- l2trans accepts.
fn: makeAdder (size_t: n) fn: (size_t: x) size_t
    fn: addN (size_t: x) size_t
        return: x + n
    return: addN

add5: makeAdder 5U
size_t: a (add5: 1)
int: ok 0
if: a = 6U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
